{
  "_comment": [
    "Rig capability R4 — energy preferences, seeded in the LEGACY grid form on purpose.",
    "",
    "minor_version is 1, so Home Assistant's own _EnergyPreferencesStore._async_migrate_func",
    "rewrites the grid source into the unified flat form (stat_energy_from / stat_energy_to)",
    "while loading it. That is why this file is written the old way: the shape the rig serves",
    "is then HA's own product rather than something a fixture author decided, and the claim",
    "'a current instance answers energy/get_prefs with the flat form' is proved by the rig",
    "instead of asserted by a comment.",
    "",
    "All five source types HA defines are present (grid, solar, battery, gas, water), because",
    "the direction a statistic represents is a property of the source type and the field it",
    "sits on — and the unit fixture that carried only the legacy grid plus solar is exactly",
    "how finding #26 stayed invisible: solar is the one type for which 'stat_energy_from means",
    "production' happens to be true.",
    "",
    "Home Assistant ignores unknown top-level keys in a .storage file, so this note travels",
    "with the fixture. Source: homeassistant/components/energy/data.py."
